{#
  Shown when .store/raw.duckdb is held by another process.

  This used to surface as a bare Flask 500 on every tab at once, with the real
  cause — DuckDB naming the holding process — buried in the server log. The one
  failure with a concrete, one-step fix deserves to say so on the page.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Database locked</title>
<style>
body{background:#0d1117;color:#c9d1d9;font-family:'Segoe UI',Consolas,monospace;padding:40px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}
h1{color:#f85149;font-size:18px;margin-bottom:14px}
.holder{background:#161b22;border:1px solid #30363d;border-left:3px solid #f85149;border-radius:6px;padding:12px 14px;margin:16px 0}
.holder .who{color:#f0f6fc;font-size:15px;font-weight:700}
.holder .pid{color:#8b949e;font-size:12px;margin-top:4px}
.fix{background:#12161c;border:1px solid #21262d;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 16px;margin:16px 0}
.fix h2{color:#58a6ff;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:8px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px}
code{background:#161b22;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:4px;padding:1px 6px;color:#79c0ff}
.why{color:#8b949e;font-size:12px;margin-top:20px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #21262d}
details{margin-top:10px}
summary{color:#8b949e;font-size:11px;cursor:pointer}
pre{background:#161b22;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:6px;padding:10px;overflow-x:auto;
    color:#8b949e;font-size:11px;margin-top:8px;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word}
</style></head><body>

<h1>The database is currently locked by another process</h1>

<div class="holder">
  <div class="who">{{ holder }}</div>
  {% if pid %}<div class="pid">PID {{ pid }}{% if holder_path %} · {{ holder_path }}{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}
</div>

<div class="fix">
  <h2>How to fix it</h2>
  {{ remedy }}
</div>

<p>No data has been lost. Every board will work again as soon as the lock is
released — nothing needs to be re-fetched.</p>

<div class="why">
  DuckDB allows one writer process at a time, so any other program holding
  <code>{{ db_path }}</code> blocks every board at once.
  {% if pid %}To see all holders: <code>lsof {{ db_path }}</code>{% endif %}
  <details>
    <summary>Show the raw driver error</summary>
    <pre>{{ detail }}</pre>
  </details>
</div>

</body></html>
